{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792329314,"nonce":"IEbsEsWahEIfDjWGfOa1os5OWIM=","title":"String.charCodeAt boxes its Null\u003cInt\u003e result on every call: a scanning loop is 20x slower than fastCodeAt","message":"Found while profiling revcomp against rayzor (05169ba). `String.charCodeAt` answers `Null\u003cInt\u003e`, and inlined into a loop it leaves a phi of `ToDyn(MemGet I16)` and null (or, once the bounds check is proven away, a phi of one box), which is then compared with `ToDyn(const)` and cast back with `SafeCast`. Each use is an allocation (`hlp_make_dyn`), a dynamic compare (`hlp_dyn_compare`) and a dynamic cast.\n\nMeasured on the Mac, 16 M characters, same loop with `charCodeAt` against `StringTools.fastCodeAt`: 385 ms against 18 ms. Revcomp: 25% of its samples were gc + hlp_make_dyn + hlp_dyn_compare.\n\nFix (branch unbox-nullable-int): an AIR pass, `UnboxNullableInt`, after scalar replacement in the O3 pipeline. A phi of nulls and boxed integers (i32, or unsigned 8/16-bit widened by `ToInt`) that is only compared with `Eq`/`NotEq` against `ToDyn(k)`, cast to int, or tested for null becomes an i32 phi with -1 for null. The compare needs a constant other than -1, the cast back is `q \u0026 !(q \u003e\u003e 31)`, and a phi with no null edge needs none of that. Anything else reading the phi leaves it alone. `ASH_NO_UNBOX=1` turns it off.\n\nWith the pass on, same binary: charCodeAt loop 385 ms -\u003e 19 ms; ReverseComplement 185 ms -\u003e 114 ms; outputs identical. Test: unbox_null (edge cases against the Haxe evaluator on every engine) and the unit tests in air.\n\nNot done: other sources of Null\u003cInt\u003e/Null\u003cFloat\u003e (Map.get, Array.pop, optional arguments) take different shapes; the same pass could be widened to them once measured.","files":null}]}